"""
Sep 19 2026: universe tiers for the new Scanner tab. NIFTY_500_STOCKS
and NIFTY_500_SECTOR_FALLBACK stay in nifty500_universe.py (unchanged,
still what Market Pulse's breadth panel uses) -- this file only adds
the NEW tiers the Scanner's universe dropdown needs.

NIFTY_50_STOCKS / NIFTY_100_STOCKS / NIFTY_200_STOCKS: NOT the
official NSE index membership -- there's no live feed for that in
this project, and re-deriving it from ANOTHER static snapshot would
just compound one stale source's own drift into a second one.
Instead: top 50/100/200 of nifty500_universe.py's own NIFTY_500_STOCKS,
ranked by REAL market_cap_cr (fundamentals_data.json, same source the
Market Heatmap's sector drawer already uses) -- an honest
approximation of "the 50/100/200 biggest names in our Nifty 500 list
today," not a claim to match NSE's own official membership (which also
weighs free-float, not raw market cap, and has its own inclusion
buffer rules this doesn't replicate).

Real gap found and handled deliberately, not glossed over: 15 of 500
symbols have no market_cap_cr in fundamentals_data.json at all,
including some genuinely large names -- LTIM (LTIMindtree) simply
isn't covered by that file's snapshot, and TATAMOTORS is a live
example of the drift nifty500_universe.py's own docstring already
warned about: Tata Motors demerged into two listings during 2026
(TMCV for commercial vehicles, TATAMOTORS now specifically Passenger
Vehicles) sometime after this project's Nov 2024 source snapshot, and
whichever entity "TATAMOTORS" pointed to when fundamentals_data.json
was built evidently isn't the one trading under that symbol now.
Ranking zero as the lowest market cap would have silently dropped
real large-caps into whatever tier a rank-500 stock lands in -- wrong
in a different, worse way than a small gap. These 15 are excluded
from the ranking entirely instead: they still appear under Nifty 500
and All Stocks, just not assigned into a 50/100/200 tier on bad data.
Excluded: BAJAJ-AUTO, GMRINFRASTRUCT, GUJGASLTD, GSPL, ISEC,
JBCHEPHARM, LTIM, MTARTECH, NAM-INDIA, PEL, RAJESHEXPO, STLTECH,
SUVENPHAR, SWANENERGY, TATAMOTORS.

ALL_NSE_STOCKS: every EQ-series symbol with an entry in
fundamentals_data.json (2,466 stocks) -- the broadest list this
project actually has real company data for. This is NOT the same
2,000-2,500-ish universe any other single reference tool might show
("861 stocks" in one seen this session) -- different tools draw this
line differently; this is simply everything OUR OWN local data covers.
Real, honest cost worth flagging up front, not discovered later:
ScannerView only has LIVE quotes/technicals cached for the ~500 names
in NIFTY_500_STOCKS (Market Pulse's own breadth cache) plus the 208
FNO_STOCKS. Selecting "All Stocks" will show real, live cards for
whichever of these 2,466 symbols overlap that ~500-2,466 window your rest
show as not-yet-loaded (never a fabricated price) rather than pretend
all 2,466 are live-scored -- that would need its own dedicated fetch
and warmup buildout, the same kind of staged rollout the Nifty 500
widening itself got, not something to bolt on silently here.
"""

